title:: Visual Server
summary:: A pattern-based visual composition system mirroring the SC audio server
categories:: Guides>VisualServer
related:: Classes/VisualServer, Classes/VisualSynthDef, Classes/Vbind, Classes/AVbind, Classes/VisualRenderer, Reference/VisualParameters

The Visual Server is a real-time visual generation framework that mirrors SuperCollider's audio server architecture, so you compose visuals with the patterns you already know (link::Classes/Pbind::, link::Classes/Pseq::, link::Classes/Pwhite::, ...).

section:: Architecture

list::
## link::Classes/VisualServer:: — manages views (windows) and nodes; server-like code::vnew::/code::vset::/code::vfree::.
## link::Classes/VisualSynthDef:: — a visual "instrument": render function + default params + envelope. Built-ins: code::\circle \square \line \pulse \spinner \live::.
## link::Classes/VisualEventTypes:: — auto-registers the event types (code::\visual \vpulse \vline \vlive \audioVisual::) at class compile (its code::*initClass::).
## link::Classes/Vbind:: (and link::Classes/Vpulse::, link::Classes/Vline::, link::Classes/Vlive::, link::Classes/AVbind::, link::Classes/Vseq::, link::Classes/Vpar::, link::Classes/Vrand::, link::Classes/Vwrand::) — pattern factories that emit visual events.
## link::Classes/VisualRenderer:: — trails, grids, particles, performance monitor.
::

Coordinates are normalised code::-1.0 .. 1.0:: relative to the view centre.

section:: Installation

This is a directory of SuperCollider classes (in code::Classes/::) plus help (code::HelpSource/::). Install by copying the whole directory into the Extensions folder.

list::
## strong::Remove any previous install first:: — delete the old code::Extensions/visualServer:: (older versions had the code::.sc:: files flat in that folder; leaving them alongside the new code::Classes/:: causes duplicate-class compile errors).
## Copy the whole directory:
::
code::
// in a terminal:
rm -rf ~/Library/Application\ Support/SuperCollider/Extensions/visualServer
cp -r /path/to/visuals/visualServer ~/Library/Application\ Support/SuperCollider/Extensions/visualServer
::
list::
## Recompile the class library (Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+L). SC compiles code::Classes/*.sc:: recursively and auto-indexes code::HelpSource/:: (these help pages). The event types auto-register via link::Classes/VisualEventTypes::'s code::*initClass:: — strong::no manual load needed::.
::

note:: code::VisualEventTypes.scd:: is now an optional no-op stub kept only so older scripts that still code::.load:: it do not error. ::

section:: Quick start

code::
(
VisualServer.default.start;
~v = VisualServer.default.createView(\demo, Rect(200, 200, 800, 600), Color.black);
)

Vbind(
    \x, Pwhite(-0.8, 0.8),
    \y, Pwhite(-0.8, 0.8),
    \size, Pexprand(20, 80),
    \color, Pfunc({ Color.hsv(1.0.rand, 0.8, 1) }),
    \dur, 0.3,
    \view, \demo
).vplay;
::

section:: Patterns and vplay

The code::V*:: classes return ordinary link::Classes/Pbind::s seeded with sensible defaults (code::\type::, code::\dur::, code::\instrument::, code::\view::); your pairs override them. This library adds code::Pattern:vplay:: which plays through a link::Classes/VpatternPlayer:: using an empty proto event (keeps SC's audio event machinery out of the visual model — see link::Classes/VpatternPlayer::). code::vplay:: returns the player; call code::.stop:: on it.

code::
p = Vbind(\instrument, \square, \dur, 0.4, \view, \demo).vplay;
p.stop;
::

section:: Live input

Any parameter value may be a link::Classes/Function::; it is evaluated every frame (for code::\live::/persistent nodes) or every event (link::Classes/LiveParam::/link::Classes/LiveStream:: inside a pattern). Use code::\dur, inf:: (or link::Classes/Vlive::) for a persistent node driven by sensor/data globals.

code::
~imu = (x: 0, y: 0);
Routine({ loop { ~imu.x = sin(thisThread.seconds); ~imu.y = cos(thisThread.seconds*0.7); 0.03.wait } }).play;
VisualServer.default.vnew(\live, nil, \demo, [\x, { ~imu.x }, \y, { ~imu.y }, \size, 70]);
::

section:: Audio-visual sync

link::Classes/AVbind:: plays an audio note and a synchronised visual per event. strong::One rule:: every visual key is code::v::-prefixed (code::\vinstrument \vx \vy \vsize \vcolor \vfill \vdur \vview \vstartSize \vendSize \vcurve \vx1 \vy1 \vx2 \vy2 \vwidth \vlength \vspeed \vattack \vrelease \vlegato \vsustain \vstretch::); the audio side keeps the plain SC note keys (incl. its own code::\legato::/code::\sustain::). link::Classes/Vbind:: is visual-only, so it uses the plain names — the prefix is only needed where audio + visual share one event. See link::Reference/VisualParameters::.

code::
s.boot;
AVbind(\instrument, \default, \freq, Pseq([440,660,880],inf), \amp, 0.2, \dur, 0.4,
    \vinstrument, \pulse, \vendSize, Pkey(\amp)*600, \vattack, 0.1, \vview, \demo).play;
::

section:: Effects

code::
r = VisualRenderer.default;
r.addTrailEffect(\demo, 0.08);
r.addGrid(\demo, 60, Color.gray(0.15));
r.addPerformanceMonitor(\demo);
// r.clearEffects(\demo);
::

section:: Envelope and overlap

Each visual node has its own attack/hold/release envelope, decoupled from the pattern's code::\dur:: (which is only the spawn spacing). The lifetime is:

code::
life = (sustain ? dur) * legato * stretch
::

The envelope drives both strong::alpha:: and strong::size scale:: (grow in / shrink out); code::\pulse:: keeps its own code::startSize->endSize:: sweep. code::life == inf:: => persistent node (never freed) — the default for code::\live:: and code::\spinner::.

list::
## Defaults (code::legato:: 1, code::stretch:: 1, code::attack:: 0, code::release:: nil, code::sustain:: nil) reproduce the original "fade over code::dur::, free at code::dur::" — no overlap.
## code::\legato:: scales the whole envelope. code::\legato, 8:: with code::\dur, 0.12:: => each node lives ~1.2 s while a new one spawns every 0.12 s => ~10 overlapping.
## code::\sustain:: sets an explicit base lifetime (seconds) regardless of code::\dur::.
## code::\attack::/code::\release:: are strong::absolute seconds:: (NOT scaled by legato/stretch) clamped into the life; the remainder is the hold. code::\curve:: shapes the segments (code::\exp::/code::\log:: are mapped to numeric curves because link::Classes/Env:: exp segments can't touch level 0).
::

In a link::Classes/Vbind:: use the plain names (code::\attack \release \legato \sustain \stretch::). In an link::Classes/AVbind:: they are code::v::-prefixed (code::\vattack \vrelease \vlegato \vsustain \vstretch::) — plain code::\legato::/code::\sustain:: there belong to the audio note.

code::
// Vbind (visual-only) - plain keys
Vbind(\x, Pwhite(-0.7,0.7), \y, Pwhite(-0.7,0.7), \size, 50,
    \color, Pfunc({ Color.hsv(1.0.rand,0.8,1) }),
    \dur, 0.12, \legato, 10, \view, \demo).vplay;          // overlapping

// AVbind - v-prefixed visual envelope
AVbind(\instrument, \default, \freq, Pwhite(300,800), \amp, 0.2,
    \dur, 0.12, \vinstrument, \circle, \vsize, 50,
    \vlegato, 10, \vattack, 0.1, \vview, \demo).play;       // overlapping
::

Full key list and defaults: link::Reference/VisualParameters::.

